Pat asked that replies end with a clear summary of the objective and
its status, the next actions he must take, and the information he must
provide, instead of questions spread through the body [1].

Patch 1 adds the rule to CLAUDE.md, beside the quoting rules, with a
fixed shape for the summary. It holds that a task is either done or
blocked on the reader, so a reply that is not done must name what
unblocks it.

Patch 2 names the summary in step 6 of the pass prompt, where a pass
writes its reply.

The series is independent of "[PATCH] src/lab-process-mail: Finish the
work within a pass" [2], which rewrites the step 4 rule for a pass
that cannot finish. The two touch different hunks of prompt.md and
apply in either order.

